{
  "question": "in the sequences InterPro calls Rieske but this database's gate excludes, which cluster ligand is substituted, and by what?",
  "why_it_matters": "a curator cannot act on '139 sequences were dropped'. Cys to Ser loses the thiolate that holds the iron; Cys to Gly suggests the fold itself is gone; His to Tyr may mean a different coordination chemistry rather than none. The substitution is the question, not the count",
  "method": {
    "alignment": "hmmalign against the project motif model ROmotif71, then insert columns removed with ro_motif.read_stockholm_matchcols so that column numbers are model positions",
    "columns": [
      {
        "column": 164,
        "accepted": "C",
        "label": "Rieske Cys-1"
      },
      {
        "column": 166,
        "accepted": "H",
        "label": "Rieske His-1"
      },
      {
        "column": 184,
        "accepted": "C",
        "label": "Rieske Cys-2"
      },
      {
        "column": 187,
        "accepted": "H",
        "label": "Rieske His-2"
      }
    ],
    "window": 2,
    "columns_are_not_restated_here": "the columns and the tolerance window are read from ro_motif, the owner of the motif question; restating them would be a second implementation of the same measurement, and this project has measured that those diverge silently",
    "changes_nothing": "this script measures and reports; no call, no table and no curation is changed by it"
  },
