  "canonical_pair_in_raw_sequence": {
    "pattern": "C.H.{10,30}C..H",
    "counts": {
      "absent": 138,
      "present": 1
    },
    "what_it_separates": "a ligand can be missed for two opposite reasons: it is genuinely absent, or it is present but displaced beyond the column test's two-position window. Those give the same result and mean opposite things -- 'this protein cannot bind the cluster' against 'our alignment misses it'. This pattern is searched in the raw sequence, independent of any alignment or column number, so it separates the two",
    "validated_on": {
      "sequences_we_call_intact": 4000,
      "of_those_matching_the_pattern": 3978,
      "share": 0.9945
    },
    "what_it_is_not": "finding the pattern does not prove a working cluster: the spacing is necessary, not sufficient, and a sequence can carry C-x-H ... C-x-x-H by chance. It narrows the question rather than answering it"
  },
